Falsifies `system_tests::user::disk_tests::the_disk_surveyor_reads_a_table_gptfdisk_wrote`, its
NVMe half (milestone 421 (the block roster names an NVMe disk)).

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is `disk_service::devices` writing the virtio disks and no NVMe entry, so a machine with
an NVMe controller attached hands `disk_surveyor` a roster that says it has none.

Expected to fail: the `nvme` count's assertion, "the surveyor lists 0 NVMe disks; NIFE_NVME is set
on this leg, so the roster owes 1", with `left: 0`, `right: 1`. Confirmed red on 2026-10-18 (UTC)
on aarch64 with `script/test --arch aarch64 --no-host --test
the_disk_surveyor_reads_a_table_gptfdisk_wrote`.

